sentences.l:
If under me, at least, a god subdues the noble suitors,
I will bring wives for you both and give you possessions,
and houses built near me;

But if indeed we are so far lacking in the strength
of godlike Odysseus, in that we cannot string
the bow;

And Eurymachus most of all and godlike-in-form Antinous
I beg, since also this word as is fitting he spoke,
now to let the bow rest, and to entrust it to the gods;

sentences.t:
οὐκ ἀγαπᾷς ὃ ἕκηλος ὑπερφιάλοισι μεθ’ ἡμῖν
δαίνυσαι, οὐδέ τι δαιτὸς ἀμέρδεαι, αὐτὰρ ἀκούεις
μύθων ἡμετέρων καὶ ῥήσιος;

sentences.l:
Wine also the Centaur, renowned Eurytion,
bewildered in the hall of great-hearted Peirithous,
when he had come to the Lapiths;

Grief seized the heroes, and through the forecourt, out of doors,
they dragged him, springing up, having cut off his ears with pitiless bronze
and his nose;

sentences.t:
ἔλπεαι, αἴ χ’ ὁ ξεῖνος Ὀδυσσῆος μέγα τόξον
ἐντανύσῃ χερσίν τε βίηφί τε ἧφι πιθήσας,
οἴκαδέ μ’ ἄξεσθαι καὶ ἑὴν θήσεσθαι ἄκοιτιν;
